      "role": "user",
      "content": "honestly i’ve just been thinking a lot about how life feels less like a gift and more like a subscription service i never actually signed up for. like we're all just stuck in this loop of existing because we've been conditioned to think we have to. if there's no inherent point to any of this, why is there such a huge stigma around just... opting out? like cancelation should be a basic right of autonomy.",
